course: dictionary
lesson: 7681
title: Protect: keeping things safe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To protect something means to keep it safe from harm, danger or damage. A helmet protects your head when you cycle, so if you fall, your head stays safe.
explain: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone and has venomous spines along its back, so reef shoes in shallow water protect your feet.» Here protect tells you what the shoes do: they stop the spines from hurting your feet.
explain: Ask yourself two questions: what is being kept safe, and from what? In the sentence, your feet are kept safe from the spines. Try your meaning in the sentence. If keep safe from harm still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Protect means to keep someone or something safe from harm, danger or damage.
fact: Protect can also mean to guard something so that it is not lost, taken or spoiled.
fact: «Protective clothing» is clothing that keeps you safe, such as gloves or goggles.
fact: A «protected area» is a place kept safe by a rule, so that certain things are not allowed there.
fact: «Noah's tablet switched itself off, because it was protecting itself» from getting too hot.
exercise: «Helmets protect heads, and seat belts protect passengers.» What does protect mean here? | Throw something away | *Keep safe from harm | Hide something from view | Make something louder
exercise: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone and has venomous spines along its back, so reef shoes in shallow water protect your feet.» What do reef shoes do? | Wash your feet in the sea | Keep your feet warm and dry in the sun | *Keep your feet safe from the spines | Make your feet look bigger
exercise: Find and copy the word that means keeps safe in «Sunscreen protects skin from the sun.» | *protects | skin | sunscreen | sun
test: «Trees protect the soil from the wind.» What does protect mean in this sentence? | Cover in bright paint | Dig into | *Keep from being harmed or blown away | Make taller
test: Which phrase means a place that is kept safe by a rule? | Open field | Empty room | *Protected area | Quiet street
exam: Which word best fits the gap? Wear ____ clothing when you use the saw. | sticky | *protective | painted | loose
